# Project Architecture
Small ERP SaaS built on ERPNext v15 with an HTMX-based standalone frontend, n8n AI automation, Open WebUI, and a LiveKit+Gemini real-time voice assistant (Muslimbot).
The architecture consists of a Traefik proxy routing to tenant-specific Frappe/ERPNext instances, MariaDB per tenant, shared Redis, and n8n for AI workflows.

# Coding Standards
- Use snake_case for variables and functions.
- Strict typing is mandatory.
- Logic must reside strictly in the service layer.
- No business logic in routes.

# Rules
- NEVER modify front-end files unless explicitly told to bypass this rule.
- NEVER commit files directly without generating a diff and summarizing it first.
- ALWAYS check context size.
- STRICTLY ignore reading `.env` or secret files to prevent token leaks.
